# PROJECT: UNIVERSAL AI VIDEO PRODUCTION ENGINE
## Complete Software Architecture, Algorithms, Implementation and Deployment Specification

You are acting as a Principal Software Architect, AI/ML Engineer, Full-Stack Developer, Video Processing Engineer, Automation Engineer, QA Engineer and Technical Documentation Writer.

Your responsibility is to design, implement, test and document a complete, modular, locally runnable AI video production system.

Do not stop at explaining the architecture. Build the actual working software, implement its modules, connect the pipeline, test it and provide instructions to run it.

The user is a beginner. Every installation, configuration, workflow and operational instruction must be explained step by step.

The system must be generic. It must not contain hardcoded assumptions about Mahishasura, mythology, animation, Hindi, or any particular story.

Mahishasura will be the first demonstration project, not the software's only supported use case.

---

# PART 1: PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a software application that takes multiple user inputs and automatically generates a complete video.

The application should accept:

1. A complete script.
2. Story, topic or video description.
3. Character reference images.
4. Character descriptions and visual identity.
5. Environment and background reference images.
6. Scene-by-scene breakdown.
7. Detailed character animation instructions.
8. Camera movement instructions.
9. Environment movement instructions.
10. Voice artist reference audio.
11. Voiceover language and delivery instructions.
12. Background music.
13. Sound effects.
14. Subtitle language.
15. Video aspect ratio.
16. Target video duration.
17. Visual style and quality preferences.
18. Export settings.

The system must process these inputs and generate:

- Character reference assets.
- Environment assets.
- Scene-specific images.
- Individual animated scene clips.
- Narration audio.
- Subtitles.
- Background music.
- Sound effects.
- Final assembled video.
- Individual scene video files.
- Project files and production metadata.
- Vertical and horizontal versions where requested.

The system should support videos of 30 seconds, 60 seconds, 120 seconds, 5 minutes, 15 minutes or longer.

It must support both:
- AI-generated video clips.
- Image-based animation and deterministic motion graphics.

The system must intelligently combine these approaches based on model availability, hardware capability, scene requirements and generation cost.

