- No reliance on Comfy Cloud credits.

The application must be designed for this hardware.

Important restrictions:

1. Do not assume that large video-generation models can run locally.
2. Do not load several large models into VRAM simultaneously.
3. Avoid unnecessary GPU memory allocation.
4. Prefer CPU processing for orchestration, metadata, subtitle generation and other lightweight tasks.
5. Use GPU acceleration only when supported and beneficial.
6. Provide low-memory execution modes.
7. Process video in short segments.
8. Allow resuming interrupted jobs.
9. Cache generated assets.
10. Avoid regenerating assets that already exist.

The system must work even when no generative video model is available.

In that case, it should generate animated videos from images using camera movements, parallax, layers, masks, particles, transitions, lighting effects and audio synchronization.

Never pretend that deterministic image animation is equivalent to fully generated character animation.

